  ('00308047-08d9-57ee-aa17-8404870d127c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00308047-08d9-57ee-aa17-8404870d127c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd20ecdae-a22e-5e2c-843d-50ee4d8a8dac'::uuid, NULL, E'She went to the mall to buy a new dress for her interview.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0031471a-5f1c-50ed-b377-3d5d62462052'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0031471a-5f1c-50ed-b377-3d5d62462052'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Little Consequence(后果很小)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 1, 4, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('0033ed8d-8c57-5982-80b0-3db3e55c6970'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0033ed8d-8c57-5982-80b0-3db3e55c6970'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hand', E'I''d like you to think for a moment about your hands and all the things you can do with them. You can use them to write or to drive. You can thread a needle, play the drums, build a wall and so on and so forth. They can be careful and precise - think of someone doing eye surgery, for example. But they can also generate huge forces. And here you might think of the sportsperson throwing a discus or lifting a heavy weight. How is it possible for our hands to be so incredibly flexible? Well, it''s all down to the extraordinary complexity of the bones, ligaments, nerves and muscles that lie beneath the skin of our hands. There are, for example, nine muscles alone controlling just one thumb. Some of these are anchored to bones within the hand, while others link to the arm.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '093cf4b1-a50d-5013-a24d-3dfc7a6394a2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The human hand is extraordinarily flexible. It enables a person to do a remarkable variety of things, some demanding great precision and others requiring considerable strength. This is because of the complex structure of nerves, muscles and ligaments that makes up a hand.', NULL, NULL),
  ('00343df5-c951-5daf-8e6a-8bee821a9f62'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00343df5-c951-5daf-8e6a-8bee821a9f62'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lost Bag', E'You and your friends had dinner at a restaurant yesterday. You think you left a bag at the restaurant. You sat at the table next to the window. You had college materials inside the bag. You call the manager of the restaurant and what would you say to the manager?', 'b9bef14e-4ca9-5af4-88ca-8014f73543fa'::uuid, NULL, E'Respected manager, I hope you are doing well.\nI would like to discuss an issue we have encountered with a lost bag at your restaurant.\nIt appears that I had dinner there yesterday and left my bag beside the window table, which contains my college materials inside.\nI would appreciate your opinion on this matter. Thank you for your consideration.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0035bf87-6a21-578f-866b-32a3edbe3eb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0035bf87-6a21-578f-866b-32a3edbe3eb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Eiffel', E'The Eiffel Tower was the tallest building in the world when it was completed in 1889. It was built for the World''s Fair to {{1}} that iron could be as strong as stone while being infinitely lighter. And in fact, the wrought-iron tower is twice as tall as the masonry Washington Monument and yet it weighs 70,000 tons less! It is repainted every seven years with 50 tons of dark brown paint.\nCalled "the father of the skyscraper," the Home Insurance Building, {{2}} in Chicago in 1885 (and demolished in 1931), was 138 feet tall and 10 stories. It was the first building to effectively employ a supporting {{3}} of steel beams and columns, allowing it to have many more windows than traditional masonry structures. But this new construction method made people worry that the building would fall down, leading the city to halt construction until they could investigate the structure''s safety. In 1929, auto tycoon Walter Chrysler took part in an intense race with the Bank of Manhattan Trust Company to build the world''s tallest skyscraper. Just when it looked like the bank had captured the {{4}} title, workers at the Chrysler Building {{5}} a thin spire hidden inside the building through the top of the roof to win the contest (subsequently losing the title four months later to the Empire State Building). Chrysler also decorated his building to mirror his cars, with hubcaps, mudguards, and hood ornaments.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.demonstrate, 2.constructed, 3.skeleton, 4.coveted, 5.jacked', NULL, NULL),
  ('0039b7d7-5255-525c-a254-db77976f341c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0039b7d7-5255-525c-a254-db77976f341c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '72b6c1ef-f418-5bb1-86b8-3247e8bd21c9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'All students join art classes in their first term.', NULL, NULL),
  ('003b63b3-e586-518a-b059-14c53d97431b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '003b63b3-e586-518a-b059-14c53d97431b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Attraction', E'Researchers report that women find a man they see with an attractive woman more desirable than unattached men. That''s according to a study in the journal Evolutionary Psychology. Researchers had two groups of female college students rate photos of men, all of whom had first been rated as being of average attractiveness. The first group of 148 women was shown pictures of those men with an attractive female. The subjects were told that the women in the photos were either a girlfriend, ex-girlfriend, cousin or adopted sister. And the subjects rated the men with the girlfriends as more desirable than the men shown with partners described as being exes or relatives.\nThe second study group of 97 students were shown average looking men with an attractive woman who was described as definitely a girlfriend. And again the women rated the men with the good-looking gals as more desirable than the single guys. Plus, the attached men were thought more likely to be more intelligent, trustworthy, humorous, wealthy and attentive.\n\nIn the research, how do women think of men in different photos?', '6caa6bcf-cf8a-5f14-8fcb-79d9860d5389'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Single men are less attractive than men with pretty girls.\nMen with girlfriends are more desirable than those with relatives.\nMen with partners are thought to be more reliable than single men.', NULL, NULL),
  ('003bd097-c042-5e0a-9cfd-9feaa9af5f7e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '003bd097-c042-5e0a-9cfd-9feaa9af5f7e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b7ef6b7d-d373-5d06-a0bb-7cc09f922240'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Fruits containing too much sugar and calories have little or no nutritional value.', NULL, NULL),
  ('00462022-f159-53b8-a153-2ce1044f5b06'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00462022-f159-53b8-a153-2ce1044f5b06'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c2669ffa-1092-5641-b142-954e9f711cf4'::uuid, NULL, E'Two leading law firms are to prepare legal actions against tobacco companies.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0046ded5-dc35-544b-8bdb-0bdba91c1eb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0046ded5-dc35-544b-8bdb-0bdba91c1eb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a3ba9782-0a69-5caf-81d3-2fb8c2f68de3'::uuid, NULL, E'Becoming a good actor requires persistence and motivation.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('004830d1-61bd-55d5-8051-80b7407f1124'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '004830d1-61bd-55d5-8051-80b7407f1124'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '304330b8-b3bc-5228-b964-39ea2d1380b3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The untapped potential of using the sun''s rays is phenomenal.', NULL, NULL),
  ('00486bc4-044f-5572-a76d-e484ba096246'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00486bc4-044f-5572-a76d-e484ba096246'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Final Project', E'You need help with your final project and want to ask your teacher for assistance. How do you approach your teacher to explain the situation and what specific points do you include to ensure you get the support you need?', '09920dfa-ae62-5ebd-a5d7-d98aaed76502'::uuid, NULL, E'Respected teacher, I hope you are doing well.\nI would like to discuss an issue we have encountered with my final project.\nIt appears that I have met some difficulties while finishing my final project, and I really need your professional guidance and help to complete it properly.\nI would appreciate your opinion on this matter. Thank you for your consideration.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0048fdf9-572e-5760-b5de-b1e4d0f1d6c3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0048fdf9-572e-5760-b5de-b1e4d0f1d6c3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Central Idea', E'The central idea of this book concerns our blindness with respect to randomness, particularly the large deviations: why do we, scientists or nonscientists, hotshots or regular Joes, tend to see the pennies instead of the dollars? Why do we keep focusing on the minutiae, not the possible significant large events, in spite of the obvious evidence of their huge influence?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('004c9975-9fe4-5b8a-8298-78ebc2437657'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '004c9975-9fe4-5b8a-8298-78ebc2437657'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mistaking Repression', E'Do you keep strong emotions bottled up inside? Perhaps you always tell the people around you that you’re all right, and that they shouldn’t worry about you, even though you’re not in the best shape. While you may appear calm on the outside, hiding your negative emotions can have a negative impact. According to clinical psychologist, Victoria Tarratt, suppressing your emotions is said to affect blood pressure, memory, and self esteem. It can also aggravate depression and anxiety in the long term. So instead of repressing how you feel, acknowledge your emotion in a safe environment. Identifying your emotion can be...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '36e70594-3b15-5128-9e6c-42d02f4b8f57'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'beneficial', NULL, NULL),
  ('00523dda-569e-5ee6-b94d-f55d62de80eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00523dda-569e-5ee6-b94d-f55d62de80eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Problem of Funding', E'The most important issue is concerned with the problem of funding. Social services receive different donations or grants from the government. However, these sums are not sufficient for the solution of all problems. The second most important issue consists in the huge spending. The money social services achieve is not enough for normal functioning. The third problem, affecting human services, is the lack of skilled and experienced employees.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('00542cd5-14e8-5049-a480-47e3d0a312cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00542cd5-14e8-5049-a480-47e3d0a312cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Omniscience', E'Omniscience may be a foible of men, but it is not so of books. Knowledge, as Johnson said, is of two {{1}} , you may know a thing yourself, and you may know where to find it. Now the amount which you may actually know yourself must, at its best, be limited, but what you may know of the {{2}} of information may, with proper training, become almost boundless. And here come the {{3}} and use of reference books-the working of one book in connection with another-and applying your own {{4}} to both. By this means we get as near to that omniscient volume which tells everything as ever we shall get, and although the single volume or work which tells everything does not exist, there is a vast number of reference books in existence, a knowledge and proper use of which is essential to every intelligent person. Necessary as I believe reference books to be, they can easily be made to be {{5}} to idleness, and too mechanical a use should not be made of them.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.kinds, 2.sources, 3.value, 4.intelligence, 5.contributory', NULL, NULL),
  ('00564a75-e7f6-5c2a-af1d-95cb501d2e31'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00564a75-e7f6-5c2a-af1d-95cb501d2e31'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Kepler-452b', E'The discovery of a new exoplanet has ignited excitement among astronomers worldwide. Dubbed Kepler-452b, this Earth-like planet orbits a star similar to our sun in the habitable zone. With a radius 1.5 times that of Earth, it offers the potential for liquid water and a stable atmosphere.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('005c91e8-184a-5be7-9f9a-54892bfeb736'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '005c91e8-184a-5be7-9f9a-54892bfeb736'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a scientific test that is done to discover or prove something?', '199fae8f-a06d-51ce-bcfe-7809721535a4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Experiment', NULL, NULL),
  ('005fcbf7-3a7c-5b85-bcb1-36a411cfbe92'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '005fcbf7-3a7c-5b85-bcb1-36a411cfbe92'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5c6d99fe-ddc1-5588-b4be-2c23adf345e2'::uuid, NULL, E'He is a hard worker and a skilled gardener who is about to retire.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0060fc1a-1d59-568c-8537-eb798fc5055f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0060fc1a-1d59-568c-8537-eb798fc5055f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Han Dynasty', E'The Han Dynasty, which flourished from 206 BCE to 220 CE in ancient China, represented a golden age of Chinese history, {{1}} by consolidation, expansion, and enduring cultural achievements. Instituting Confucianism as the official state philosophy, the Han fostered a civil service system that {{2}} officials based on merit rather than birthright—a radical departure from previous aristocratic norms. This {{3}} was defined by innovations such as papermaking, which revolutionized record-keeping and literacy, and the codification of traditional medicinal practices. The Silk Road, an elaborate network of trade routes {{4}} during this period, opened China to cultural exchanges and commerce with the Mediterranean world. Venerated for stabilizing the internal order and external borders, the Han Dynasty’s governance provided a model for future Chinese rulers. This prospering period in East Asian history is still considered a benchmark for Chinese civilization, with the ethnic majority of China today {{5}} to themselves as the ‘Han people.’', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.distinguished, 2.selected, 3.epoch, 4.established, 5.referring', NULL, NULL),
  ('00640ca4-b82a-5f1a-8fa4-397b52bafa94'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00640ca4-b82a-5f1a-8fa4-397b52bafa94'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Culture Hearths', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 4, 1, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('00676c17-287e-55f7-bf15-d8f60ea137f6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '00676c17-287e-55f7-bf15-d8f60ea137f6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WorldWide Telescope', E'If you''ve ever wanted to explore the universe, your dream is now as close as your keyboard. Because last week, Microsoft unveiled its online WorldWide Telescope. The program was developed in partnership with NASA and research institutions such as the California Institute of Technology. The WorldWide Telescope uses the best high-resolution imagery that''s been {{1}} both here on earth and in space. The images are joined together to put celestial objects in the correct perspective and in their actual {{2}} in the sky.\nFrom your computer, you can peer through telescopes such as the Hubble or the Chandra X-Ray Observatory. You can roam on your own through the galaxies, get up close and {{3}} with the planets, or take tours {{4}} by astronomers and professors. You can choose to look through different wavelengths of light to reveal hidden structures. And you can explore the heavens not only as they are today, but as they were in the past or will be in the future. The late Jim Gray, a Microsoft computer scientist, conceived of this effort as a way to make the universe accessible to everyone. The free program can be {{5}} at worldwidetelescope.org.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.generated, 2.positions, 3.personal, 4.guided, 5.downloaded', NULL, NULL),
  ('006e5d97-595c-511b-8027-f0724224d0d7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '006e5d97-595c-511b-8027-f0724224d0d7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Where do we see aquatic animals?', '152eaa87-5415-555b-930c-c5c24b91c9a0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Aquarium / water', NULL, NULL),
  ('006f3d15-ecc9-5563-8758-6d013bd95305'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '006f3d15-ecc9-5563-8758-6d013bd95305'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Communication Change', E'The means of communicating in society today has changed greatly over the last ten years. Is it a positive or negative change?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('006fd908-5648-57d5-9a1a-7de82af3335a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '006fd908-5648-57d5-9a1a-7de82af3335a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tour Guide', E'The best way to travel is in a group led by a tour guide. To what extent do you agree with this statement?', NULL, NULL, E'The debate over whether traveling in a group led by a tour guide is the best way to travel has been ongoing for years. While some people believe that group travel provides a safer and more enriching travel experience, I believe that independent travel is more fulfilling. This essay will argue that group travel can be restrictive, limiting the ability to explore at one''s own pace, and may provide a biased or narrow perspective of the destination.\nTraveling in a group can be restrictive and limit the ability to explore at one''s own pace. Group travel often has a set itinerary that may not align with individual preferences or interests. Additionally, group travel may not provide enough time to fully explore a destination, as time is often allotted for group activities and tours.\nA tour guide may provide a biased or narrow perspective of the destination, limiting the travel experience. Tour guides may have their own agendas or biases that can influence the information they provide about a destination. Additionally, tour guides may only take travelers to popular tourist destinations, limiting exposure to lesser-known but equally interesting sites.\nIn conclusion, I believe that traveling in a group led by a tour guide is not the best way to travel. While some may argue that group travel provides a safer and more enriching travel experience, it can be restrictive and limit the ability to explore at one''s own pace. Additionally, tour guides may provide a biased or narrow perspective of the destination, limiting the travel experience. Independent travel allows for more flexibility and freedom to explore at one''s own pace, leading to a more fulfilling and personalized travel experience.', NULL, 200, 300),
